Subject: [TEST builds only] clk: qcom: gcc-sm8550: let pcie_0_gdsc collapse in system suspend

Test builds only.  scripts/build-mainline-kernel.sh applies this only with
APPLY_SM8550_PCIE0_GDSC_OFF=1, after gcc-sm8550-usb-gdscs-retention.patch,
refuses it without APPLY_SM8550_SLEEP_FIXES=1, and refuses a build without
the variable in a source tree that carries it.  No board check: both
tablets' builds get it when the variable is set.

pcie_0_gdsc goes from PWRSTS_RET_ON to PWRSTS_OFF_ON.  gdsc_disable() then
drops the application processor's vote for it (it is VOTABLE, and probe
clears GDSC_SLEEP_ENA_VOTE) when genpd powers it off at the end of a
suspend's noirq phase, instead of leaving it on in hardware until CX
collapses.  Nothing else changes: pcie_0_phy_gdsc, the PCIe1 domains and
the USB domains keep their states, and the line count of the file is the
same, so the patches after this one apply at the same lines.

Why.  On the SM-X710 (gts9wifi) a sleep with the PCIe host powered down
(its root port removed, so that dw_pcie_suspend_noirq() takes its power-off
branch) and the interconnect floor released did not return with this GDSC
in retention: 0 of 8 (six on Type-C kit revision 7's kernel, one on
revision 9's, one on revision 10's), the SoC dropping PS_HOLD 43 to 44 s
after the RTC alarm; the same sleep with the floor held came back.  With the
GDSC collapsed it returned 7 of 7 (four on revision 9, three on revision 10,
through the run-time switch of gcc-sm8550-gdsc-debug-switches.patch), and
with revision 10's PIPE clock revert the PCIe host came back as well.  Two
SM8550 community kernels with the same symptom made the same change
(ROCKNIX PR 3636, retroforge patch 0143).

Why upstream has PWRSTS_RET_ON (967e011013ed, "clk: qcom: gcc-sm8550: Do
not turn off PCIe GDSCs during gdsc_disable()", v6.14): a PCIe controller
that keeps its link through a system suspend (qcom_pcie_suspend_noirq()
with the link kept, the PCI devices still bound) loses its registers when
its GDSC collapses, and its resume breaks.  That is the case on this port in
every suspend in which the Wi-Fi stays: the root port cannot go to D3, so
dw_pcie_suspend_noirq() keeps the link, and genpd still powers the GDSC off.
The boot's pm_test=platform panel cycle is such a suspend.  This patch does
nothing about it; it is for testing the sleep with the PCIe host powered
down.

It needs the PIPE clock revert (clk-qcom-regmap-phy-mux-revert-rework.patch,
APPLY_SM8550_SLEEP_FIXES=1): without it the GDSC did not report power-up at
the resume ("pcie_0_gdsc status stuck at 'off'", revision 9).

--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8550.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8550.c
@@ -3003,7 +3003,7 @@
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "pcie_0_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON, /* gcc-sm8550-pcie0-gdsc-off-in-suspend.patch */
 	.flags = VOTABLE | POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE,
 };

